// "Bourg Bouillotte": a little hill town at the blue hour, its windows lit (issue #168, the 13th
// circuit, the first of the fourth cup), after the guide « Conception des circuits »
// (docs/GAME_DESIGN.md § 16). Original layout, about 1590 m a lap, turning right, from 7 to 33 m
// up: the start straight on the market square, 10 m up; a hairpin to the right down into the
// lower town and a hairpin to the left round the washhouse, 7 m up; the climb north up the
// rampart's street (31 %, in anti-gravity) to the top of the town; the risky jump's corner on
// the top, 33 m up (a tight corner to the right, its inside a drop down to the gardens, that a
// ramp crosses), its wide landing, south; then the lacets down through the town, four hairpins
// (left, right, left, right): the belfry's terrace and its drop of 4 m, the bakers' street;
// the bulge round a giant belfry, whose hidden road runs straight behind a stack of the market's
// crates; the last corner, that the grass bridge crosses behind a panel that breaks under a boost;
// a bump on the way back to the line. Six hairpins of 180° (a Normal bot drifts them), the
// bulge's S (left 75°, right 150°, left 75°), four tight corners of 90°: no long soft curve, one
// long straight. The pieces of the shortcuts (the jump's corner and its landing; the last
// hairpin, the bulge, the last corner and their paths) are the Coteau Citrouille's (the Corniche
// Cannelle's, issues #107, #156: their gains and their hiding were tuned), with other covers; the
// rest is new.
//
// Drawn as a plan of straights and arcs, its points every 8 m along it (the parameters below
// follow them).
//
// Format: see src/track/data.rs. Point 0 is the start line; karts drive toward point 1 (north,
// -Z), then turn right. The grid sits on the straight behind point 0.
(
    name: "Bourg Bouillotte",
    // Dressing (issue #11): the hill town at the blue hour (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), the same
    // every time (seed), and pieces placed by hand: checkered flags at the start line, a giant
    // belfry that hides the hidden road, a giant tower by the jump's corner.
    biome: "Bourg",
    // Issue #104: its music (`assets/data/music.ron`).
    music: "cool-city",
    decor_seed: 168,
    // Issue #195: the town's hill (`assets/data/biomes.ron`), and it hugs the road (`embank`, rise
    // over run: about 31°, as on the circuits of issue #211): the road, 7 to 33 m above the
    // valley, is carried by the hill up to its walls, instead of skirts down to the valley. The
    // voids stay (the jump's corner, the bulge, the last corner: 6 m under the road at least).
    terrain: (height: 34.0, scale: 140.0, floor: 0.25, rock: (0.52, 0.46, 0.42), embank: 0.6),
    props: [
        (model: "racing-kit/flagCheckers", at: 0.0, side: Both, height: 4.0, radius: 0.9, gap: 1.8),
        (model: "castle-kit/tower-slant-roof", at: 166.216, side: Right, height: 24.0, radius: 3.8, gap: 8.0),
        (model: "castle-kit/tower-square-roof", at: 61.204, side: Left, height: 14.0, radius: 6.0, gap: 2.0),
    ],
    checkpoint_spacing: 25.0,
